# Volt sports nose and door handles — 2026-10-31

After the previous nose was rejected, the hood, front fascia and side corners were reshaped together. The hood descends toward a lower leading edge; upper-fascia projection and the corner turn were revised, and the lower lip no longer rises sharply in the middle. Both pairs of flush handles now sit near the trailing edge of their respective doors. The car's handling and wheel placement were not changed.

The actual full/simple model measurements show the upper fascia protruding about 26.7/25.1 mm beyond the hood edge versus 90.0/83.5 mm at task start. Measured front corner radii are about 123.6/127.4 mm versus 62.9/64.1 mm. These figures use model authoring coordinates and do not substitute for visual acceptance.

Final procedural and prepared checks passed: retained nose 10/10, sports nose 8/8, optics 16/16, redesign 149/149 and 150/150, door shape 100/100, handles 30/30, and seam checks 34/34. The sports nose test rejects the task-start geometry; the handle test rejects the old centered handle placement. All 453 same-process prepared mesh arrays match procedural arrays; source hashes in the baked manifest match. The actual-kit Garage-template regression passes 24/24, and the actual Compatibility Garage/race test passes 58/58. That test logged several frame hitches, so it is not a performance measurement.

Both desktop Compatibility and desktop Mobile captured 18 clean/worn views. Inspected final [side](evidence/volt-sports-nose-2026-10-31/final-gl_compatibility/side-opposite-clean.png), [front three-quarter](evidence/volt-sports-nose-2026-10-31/final-gl_compatibility/front-quarter-high-clean.png), and [door handles](evidence/volt-sports-nose-2026-10-31/handles/right.png). The front remains simpler than the reference and appearance acceptance remains open.

The Electric meshes, racing shadows, all six Garage templates, and Electric picture assets were rebuilt. Godot editor import returned successfully and logged an unavailable Android build-tools directory. No Android build or device test was performed. Sandbox test runs logged nonfatal Windows root-certificate warnings.
